From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: shell32: files dragged between folders move, and the views show it

Dragging files in File Explorer and to and from the desktop, as on Windows:

- two or more files moved into a folder that exists were not moved at all:
  SHFileOperation(FO_MOVE) returned ERROR_CANCELLED whenever there were more
  sources than targets (Windows moves them into the folder);
- a file dragged a little way in its own folder was copied ("... - Copy");
  now nothing happens unless Ctrl is held, and a folder never drops into
  itself or a folder inside it;
- the same drive letter is the same drive for a drop's default move: a
  profile folder linked elsewhere (Desktop, Documents) is still on C:, where
  GetVolumePathName names the link's target -- files dragged from Documents
  to the Desktop were copied;
- a move is a rename from one folder to another: the change notice only
  reached watchers of the folder the file left, so the folder it went to did
  not show it; the view now adds it (in sort order) or takes it away;
- the view a drag started in takes out the files that are gone when the drag
  ends (the drop may have moved them in another process, whose change
  notices never reach this one);
- over a folder the drop would go into, the view draws it highlighted
  (LVIS_DROPHILITED); over the dragged items themselves or over a file that
  takes no drop, the drop goes to the folder itself;
- CF_HDROP for items given as full ID lists (the desktop's icons from the
  user's and the public Desktop together) named the root's first child.

Gate: make test-drag.
